MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Different Shades Of Blue and The Breeze fit the blues direction I want now; Old Sock makes the relaxed blues tribute especially appealing.",
    "Hypnotic Eye feels like a natural continuation after You Should Be So Lucky, while Gary Clark Jr. Live connects with my interest in Hendrix's guitar playing."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The Lumineers' folk-pop direction misses the blues guitar and classic rock I want today, even though acoustic or roots-oriented music might seem related.",
    "Supernova does not give me as clear a connection to my current interests as the three albums I chose. Other compatible albums can still wait because I only want a few listens now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "A broad roots-oriented connection seems to count too much; roots rock, folk-pop, and blues do not satisfy the same listening mood for me.",
    "Familiar classic-rock territory alone is not enough to make something an immediate choice, as with the Loggins & Messina collection."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My current preference is specifically for blues guitar and relaxed blues, rather than everything adjacent to classic rock.",
    "There is a difference between something I would enjoy eventually and something I would choose today: Gary Clark Jr. Live interests me, but The Breeze has the stronger immediate pull."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my blues and classic-rock interests, but stretch that connection too broadly and sometimes mistake general interest for an immediate choice."
}
